{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"TrackingPlans"}],"title":"TrackingPlans","externalID":"TrackingPlans","symbolKind":"module","role":"collection"},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Making a plan","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/File","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanError"],"anchor":"Making-a-plan"},{"title":"Writing a plan","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/files","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/files(carryingForward:)","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/write(to:)","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanCommand"],"anchor":"Writing-a-plan"},{"title":"Checking a plan","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/check(against:)","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/check(againstDirectory:)","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanCheck","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanDifference"],"anchor":"Checking-a-plan"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/trackingplans"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Export every event an app tracks as JSON Schema that people and services outside the app can read, and check each change against the plan committed before it.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A tracking plan is the contract between an app and whoever reads its events: dashboards, a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"warehouse, a collector, another platform’s client. Each event’s document gives its version,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"consent category, properties and their JSON types, which ones every payload holds, and which are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", in a form that needs no Swift to read. Committed beside the events, it puts every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"change to them in the pull request as a JSON diff. Its check says which changes break what has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"already shipped: payloads from installed app versions that a validating collector would reject,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and stored records the app could no longer decode.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan"},{"text":" turns events’ schemas into files: an index, ","type":"text"},{"code":"tracking-plan.json","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and for each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event a JSON Schema (draft 2020-12) document and an example payload. The files are values, so the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same schemas give the same bytes on every run and platform, ready to commit for the people and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tools outside the app.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Checking compares the plan the events make now with the committed one by what the files mean. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanCheck"},{"type":"text","text":" is a match, a plan that is only out of date, or one with a breaking"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"difference: a change that, at the same version, would leave a stored record or an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"already-released app’s payload unable to decode or validate. Each "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanDifference"},{"type":"text","text":" names"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the event, the property and the change, and says whether it is breaking."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Only code compiled against the app’s event types can read their schemas, so the app writes a small"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"executable of its own: a type that conforms to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanCommand","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", marked "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@main"},{"type":"text","text":". It writes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the plan to a directory, or checks it with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"check"},{"type":"text","text":". To run the check from the app’s tests instead,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlanTesting"},{"type":"text","text":". The schemas usually come from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventMacros"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The module is a product of its own that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves out."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import TrackingPlans","import Traffluent","","@Event(name: \"signed_up\")","struct SignedUp {","    var plan: String","}","","let plan = try TrackingPlan(schemas: [SignedUp.schema])","let check = plan.check(against: plan.files)  \/\/ .matches","let paths = plan.files.map(\\.path)","\/\/ [\"tracking-plan.json\", \"signed_up.v1.schema.json\", \"signed_up.v1.example.json\"]"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers the executable, the command plugins and the test.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://TrackingPlans/documentation/TrackingPlans/TrackingPlan/schemas":{"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"schemas","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"EventSchema","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events11EventSchemaV"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/trackingplans\/trackingplan\/schemas","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"schemas","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The plan’s event schemas, ordered by the UTF-8 bytes of their names and then by version."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/schemas"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/trackingplanworkflow":{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Exporting and Checking a Tracking Plan"}],"title":"Exporting and Checking a Tracking Plan"},"doc://TrackingPlans/documentation/TrackingPlans/TrackingPlan/check(against:)":{"title":"check(against:)","abstract":[{"text":"Compares the plan with ","type":"text"},{"code":"committed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the files of a plan exported before, and reports every","type":"text"},{"